    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i feel like the \"consumer protection\" argument is often just a smokescreen used to justify keeping these massive barriers to entry in place. if you actually look at the data, most of these \"safety\" rules just end up being entry costs that only the monopolies can pay. don't you think it's a bit disingenuous to present both sides as equally valid when one side is basically just a mechanism for protecting big corporations from new competition?",
